# Deny by default. The relay image needs five Python files; everything else in
# this repo is either irrelevant to it or must never leave the machine.
#
# This matters more than a normal .dockerignore. `az acr build` uploads the
# build context to a registry in the cloud, and this repo root contains
# `secrets/chrome-profile/` - a logged-in Yahoo browser session, ~500 MB of
# cookies and tokens - plus `data/captures/`, which is over a gigabyte of
# recordings of a real draft room. Neither belongs in a container build, let
# alone in a registry. An allow-list is the only form that stays safe when
# someone later edits the Dockerfile.
*
!src

# Nothing under src/ is sensitive (it is the public package), but keep the
# image clean anyway.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
